      "say": "Now look at the map and the Royal Road. It ran about 2,700 kilometres from Sardis in Anatolia, today's Turkey, to Susa in Iran, with roads on to Babylon and Persepolis. Relay riders with fresh horses at each station carried messages in about a week. Herodotus wrote admiringly of these couriers. What modern system does that relay remind you of?",
